              At any time. With the Store app, press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>Caps Lock</kbd> or
              right-click the AG tray icon to turn it off, and uninstall it like any other app. With the EXE,
              macOS or Linux versions, simply select your previous layout again in your system settings.
              Your original keyboard layout is never modified.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="mb-2">
          <summary class="p-3 font-semibold cursor-pointer rounded-md border bg-card">
            Is it free?
          </summary>
          <div class="card mt-2 rounded-tl-0 rounded-tr-0">
            <p class="mb-0 text-secondary">
              Yes. AZERTY Global is free and open source (EUPL 1.2), with no account, no telemetry and no hidden cost.
              The source code is on <a href="https://github.com/AMCF-asso" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="mb-2">
          <summary class="p-3 font-semibold cursor-pointer rounded-md border bg-card">
            Do I need to buy a new keyboard?
          </summary>
          <div class="card mt-2 rounded-tl-0 rounded-tr-0">
            <p class="mb-0 text-secondary">
              No. AZERTY Global works with your current AZERTY keyboard: it only changes what the keys produce
              on screen. Stickers or a printable reference card can help over the first few days, but they are optional.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

